This function in C++ is for checking if a number is prime or not. Can you create a driver/main function that will use it and print to the console the first 20 prime numbers?

using namespace std;

bool isPrime(int n)
{
      if(n == 1 || n == 0) return false;

      for(int i = 2; i < n; i++)
      {
        if(n % i == 0) return false;
      }
      return true;
}

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

bool isPrime(int n)
{
      if(n == 1 || n == 0) return false;

      for(int i = 2; i < n; i++)
      {
        if(n % i == 0) return false;
      }
      return true;
}

int main() {
    int count = 0;
    int num = 2; // Start checking from the first prime number

    cout << "The first 20 prime numbers are:" << endl;

    while (count < 20) {
        if (isPrime(num)) {
            cout << num << " ";
            count++;
        }
        num++;
    }

    cout << endl;
    return 0;
}
```

To solve the quadratic equation $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ (where $a \neq 0$), we use the quadratic formula. The solutions for $x$ are determined by the coefficients $a$, $b$, and $c$.

The general solution is given by:

$$
x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
$$

Here is the complete derivation and solution formatted in \LaTeX:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}

\begin{document}

\section*{Solution to the Quadratic Equation}

Given the quadratic equation:
\begin{equation}
    ax^2 + bx + c = 0, \quad a \neq 0
\end{equation}

The roots of the equation are found using the quadratic formula. First, we calculate the discriminant, $\Delta$:
\begin{equation}
    \Delta = b^2 - 4ac
\end{equation}

The nature of the roots depends on $\Delta$:
\begin{itemize}
    \item If $\Delta > 0$, there are two distinct real roots.
    \item If $\Delta = 0$, there is exactly one real root (a repeated root).
    \item If $\Delta < 0$, there are two complex conjugate roots.
\end{itemize}

The general solution for $x$ is:
\begin{equation}
    x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
\end{equation}

Thus, the two possible values for $x$ are:
\begin{align}
    x_1 &= \frac{-b + \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\
    x_2 &= \frac{-b - \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
\end{align}

\end{document}
```

